comments.body:
No need for separate template instantiations for each derived type:

```cpp
inline std::ostream& operator<<(std::ostream& os, const FeeFrac& ff)
{
    return os << strprintf("FeeFrac(fee=%d, size=%d)", ff.fee, ff.size);
}
```

And then you can also move the implementation to the source file forward declare `FeeFrac` in the header.

