comments.body:
Why is this pair thing needed? Seems to be a single test-only thing? So either this should be moved to that test, or maybe pair should be handled generally, like the existing optional:

```cpp
template <typename T>
inline std::ostream& operator<<(std::ostream& os, const std::optional<T>& v)
{
    return v ? os << *v
             : os << "std::nullopt";
}
```

Either would allow dropping the includes for this.

